# What must never reach the image (M16).
#
# Without this file, `COPY app ./app` is fine but every earlier `COPY . .` — and
# the build context transfer itself — carries whatever happens to be in the
# working tree. Three things matter here:
#
#   .env          real credentials, and the one that would be a breach
#   var/          uploaded documents: other people's data in an image you push
#   .venv/        a macOS virtualenv, useless in a Linux image and ~400MB of it
#
# The rest is build speed and cache hygiene.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

var/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
tests/
